WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.741
OpenRouter off-boards

00:00:01.553 --> 00:00:02.967
three inference providers

00:00:02.791 --> 00:00:04.182
after the canary-prompt

00:00:03.994 --> 00:00:05.019
leak findings

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:06.764
Following security

00:00:06.576 --> 00:00:07.660
research showing some

00:00:07.472 --> 00:00:08.663
inference providers

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:09.335
did not honor

00:00:09.147 --> 00:00:10.373
their data policies

00:00:10.574 --> 00:00:11.752
OpenRouter removed

00:00:11.564 --> 00:00:12.825
three providers and

00:00:12.637 --> 00:00:15.007
pulled 125 endpoints

00:00:14.866 --> 00:00:15.986
from Zero Data

00:00:15.951 --> 00:00:17.366
Retention eligibility

00:00:17.902 --> 00:00:19.104
OpenRouter says the

00:00:18.916 --> 00:00:20.201
findings showed no

00:00:20.013 --> 00:00:21.333
breach of OpenRouter

00:00:21.145 --> 00:00:21.911
itself

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:22.804
The results of

00:00:22.616 --> 00:00:23.854
this testing revealed

00:00:23.666 --> 00:00:24.809
new findings about

00:00:24.621 --> 00:00:25.658
specific inference

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:26.330
providers

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:27.872
Its post links

00:00:27.684 --> 00:00:28.780
provider statements

00:00:28.592 --> 00:00:29.452
from Novita

00:00:29.582 --> 00:00:31.032
Phala and Together

00:00:31.171 --> 00:00:32.291
Earlier this week

00:00:32.197 --> 00:00:33.529
security researchers

00:00:33.341 --> 00:00:34.626
reported that certain

00:00:34.438 --> 00:00:35.581
inference providers

00:00:35.393 --> 00:00:36.855
had data compromised

00:00:36.678 --> 00:00:37.845
or otherwise shown

00:00:37.657 --> 00:00:38.376
evidence

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:39.924
Full story on

00:00:39.735 --> 00:00:40.631
the dashboard
